    "text": "I labelled 1 column for job 1, but the file is not really a one-column file. The vendor sent semicolon-separated data under a comma-delimited contract, so the whole header line arrived as a single column (`column_1` in the profile). That column contains nine fields: member_id, first_name, last_name, dob, sex, plan_code, coverage_start, coverage_end and patient_ref. I labelled it `phi: true` with role `other` because it holds names, date of birth and patient_ref. The contract writer will need to see the individual fields, and the vendor should resend the file with commas or the feed should be configured for semicolons. I did not change anything.",
